# OP2200H bring-up

RAM boot only. No flash, `saveenv`, `erase`, NAND/UBI writes. Do not unlock radios or start hostapd unless the current experiment says so.

The Mac has no built-in Ethernet. USB dongle is `en7` (Realtek, `00:e0:4c:36:09:c7`). `ifconfig en7 media 100baseTX` is unsupported. Working recipe:

```sh
sudo ipconfig set en0 DHCP
sudo ipconfig set en7 MANUAL 192.168.1.7 255.255.255.0
sudo ifconfig en7 up
ifconfig en7
route -n get default | grep interface
route -n get 192.168.1.3 | grep interface
```

Expect: `en7` `inet 192.168.1.7` and `status: active`; default route on `en0`; `192.168.1.3` (U-Boot) on `en7`.

U-Boot: `ipaddr=192.168.1.3`, `serverip=192.168.1.7`. TFTP file is often root-owned at `/private/tftpboot/op2200h-pcie-test.bin`.

If ping to the OpenWrt address fails, check the route for **that** address (`192.168.1.12` is not `192.168.1.3`). If `en0` is also `192.168.1.0/24`, packets go out Wi-Fi unless a host route points at `en7`:

```sh
route -n get 192.168.1.12 | grep interface
sudo route add -host 192.168.1.12 -interface en7
```

The case-sensitive build tree is `/private/tmp/op2200h-build-volume/openwrt`. Git uses `luna_*` names; the image compiles `pcie-rtl960x.c` and `rtl960x_eth.c`. Patch the compiled filenames in the build tree, copy into `linux-6.18.31/`, `rm` the `.o`, then rebuild. Give OpenWrt commands after a rebuild; do not re-paste the TFTP/`bootm` triplet unless those steps change. Still give the expected TFTP hash.
